[APPENDIX] Rules on the Ethics Inspector General of the Supreme Court, Assisting Organizations and Allocation of Duties [Table] <Amended on August 29, 2024>

Table of Duties Allocated to the Ethics Inspector General of the Supreme Court and Assisting Organizations

Ethics Inspector General — Chief Deliberation Officer for Ethics and Audit:
Assisting the Ethics Inspector General in the performance of duties.

Ethics and Audit Deliberation Officer No. 1:
1. Matters concerning disciplinary action against judges;
2. Investigation of misconduct by judges (including handling complaints and petitions concerning judges designated by the Ethics Inspector General);
3. Matters concerning judicial ethics;
4. Duties designated by the Ethics Inspector General.

Ethics and Audit Officer No. 1:
1. Matters concerning registration of property of judges and court staff;
2. Matters concerning restrictions on employment of retired public officials, etc.;
3. Handling complaints and petitions concerning judges.

Ethics and Audit Deliberation Officer No. 2:
1. Investigation and handling of complaints and misconduct concerning court staff, enforcement officers, judicial scriveners, etc., and analysis of causes thereof;
2. Matters concerning disciplinary action against court staff;
3. Matters concerning prevention of corruption and prohibition of improper solicitation;
4. Planning and conducting general administrative audits (excluding administrative audits in which a Justice of the Supreme Court serves as auditor), special audits, service discipline audits, and other audits specially ordered by the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court, and handling related matters;
5. Matters concerning accounting audits.
